    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74989.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely Delaney, but I have some more things to discuss, not talking about weather, but talking about some legislation. A bipartisan group of US senators earlier today introduced legislation that would increase access to gas with a higher ethanol blend after a recent court decision knocked down a Trump era rule that had allowed expanded sales of the fuel. This bill is an attempt to boost demand for corn based ethanol and inject certainty into a market that was quote unquote rocked by the court ruling. The bill would extend a waiver that would allow year round sales of 15% ethanol fuel blend known of course as E15. The EPA extended a similar waiver in 2019. However, the U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit ruled in early July that the EPA exceeded its authority by lifting the summertime restrictions on the sale of E15. And some groups are already showing their support for this. In particular, we're talking about the American Coalition for Ethanol because they endorse this congressional action to enable E15 sales year round. But I'm going to keep paying attention to this, see what the industry is saying, see what some more congressional leaders are saying. But that is all",
