    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74989.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "it's a well known fact that four companies control 80% of the makes the food supply. That four companies isn't very many. Those companies, CEOs could literally go out in the golf course and determine what they were gonna pay and what they were in charge for beef. That's not what should be happening. We need to have capitalism, we need to have competition. So the markets for our cow-capped producers are small and medium-sized feeders. Oftentimes end up where the Packers are making all the money and in these guys can't turn a profit when there's profit to be turned Okay, and the consumers on the other end are getting the raw end of the deal That's been going on for a long time What has really taken this to a whole new level is what happened here about a month month and a half ago when JBS got attacked a cyber attack from a Russian operative And I will tell you that opened another set of eyes. And that is if you only have four companies that control 80% of the food supply. And bad actors want to do harm to this country. What better way to do it than to disrupt our food supply? And all you have to do is disrupt one company and you've disrupted 40% of the food supply when it comes to meat in this country. So those two issues together make somebody that's a U.S. Senator from Montana, who's familiar with agriculture, get hit over the head of the baseball bat and say, hey man, you guys, time is at the essence here. You need to do something. Because not only is the consolidation in the packer industry, hurt in consumers and hurt in people in production agriculture, but it also puts this country at risk from a cyber attack standpoint. So, you know, I've been aware of these issues for a long time and, in fact, have done a number of things trying to reduce the consolidation agriculture. But I think what has just transpired over the last three or four months shows that there's some urgency here and we need to get after it.",
